text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures able to block target creature this turn do so.\\nFerocious — That creature gains indestructible until end of turn if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', 'All creatures get -2/-2 until end of turn. Whenever a creature dies this turn, you gain 1 life.', 'Arc Lightning deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three targets.', "Arrow Storm deals 4 damage to any target.\\nRaid — If you attacked this turn, instead Arrow Storm deals 5 damage to that permanent or player and the damage can't be prevented.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, discard a card.\\nDraw two cards.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, surveil 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may pay {2}{B}. If you do, return a creature card at random from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains flying, trample, and haste. Exile that card at the beginning of your next end step. If it would leave the battlefield, exile it instead of putting it anywhere else.', 'Attacking creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Barrage of Boulders deals 1 damage to each creature you don't control.\\nFerocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, creatures can't block this turn.", 'Bloodfell Caves enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Bloodfell Caves enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', "Bloodsoaked Champion can't block.\\nRaid — {1}{B}: Return Bloodsoaked Champion from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only if you attacked this turn.", 'Blossoming Sands enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Blossoming Sands enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', "Briber's Purse enters the battlefield with X gem counters on it.\\n{1}, {T}, Remove a gem counter from Briber's Purse: Target creature can't attack or block this turn.", 'Bring Low deals 3 damage to target creature. If that creature has a +1/+1 counter on it, Bring Low deals 5 damage to it instead.', "Burn Away deals 6 damage to target creature. When that creature dies this turn, exile its controller's graveyard.", 'Choose one or both —\\n• Tap target creature.\\n• Winterflame deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'Choose one —\\n• Destroy target monocolored creature.\\n• Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n• Draw two cards, then discard a card.', 'Choose one —\\n• Exile target creature with power 3 or greater.\\n• You draw two cards and you lose 2 life.\\n• Distribute two +1/+1 counters among one or two target creatures.', 'Choose one —\\n• Mardu Charm deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n• Create two 1/1 white Warrior creature tokens. They gain first strike until end of turn.\\n• Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature, nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', "Choose one —\\n• Put target creature on top of its owner's library.\\n• Jeskai Charm deals 4 damage to target opponent or planeswalker.\\n• Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain lifelink until end of turn.", "Choose one —\\n• Target creature you control gets +1/+1 until end of turn. It fights target creature you don't control.\\n• Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.\\n• Creatures with power 3 or less can't block this turn.", 'Choose up to one creature. Destroy the rest.', 'Counter target creature spell. Put two +1/+1 counters on up to one target creature.', 'Counter target noncreature spell unless its controller pays {1}.\\nFerocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, counter that spell instead.', "Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}. Mindswipe deals X damage to that spell's controller.", 'Counter target spell with mana value 4 or greater.', 'Counter target spell.', 'Crackling Doom deals 2 damage to each opponent. Each opponent sacrifices a creature with the greatest power among creatures that player controls.', "Crater's Claws deals X damage to any target.\\nFerocious — Crater's Claws deals X plus 2 damage instead if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.", 'Create an X/X black and green Spirit Warrior creature token, where X is the greatest toughness among creatures you control.', 'Create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'Create three 1/1 white Warrior creature tokens.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+0.\\nWhenever a Warrior you control deals combat damage to a player, you may pay 1 life. If you do, draw a card.', 'Creatures you control get +2/+1 until end of turn. Warrior creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by those Warriors also causes their controller to gain that much life.)', 'Creatures you control have haste.\\nWhenever a creature with power 4 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.', 'Creatures you control have vigilance.\\nEach creature you control can block an additional creature each combat.', 'Creatures your opponents control get -4/-0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Deathtouch\\nFerocious — Whenever Heir of the Wilds attacks, if you control a creature with power 4 or greater, Heir of the Wilds gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Deathtouch\\nMorph—Reveal a black card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Ruthless Ripper is turned face up, target player loses 2 life.', 'Defender, flying\\nMorph {U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Defender\\n{1}{B}, {T}: Each opponent loses 1 life.', "Defender\\n{1}{G}, Sacrifice another creature: You gain life equal to the sacrificed creature's toughness.", 'Defender\\n{1}{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nCreate X tapped 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nDeathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nDestroy target creature.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nDraw three cards.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nFlying', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nFlying\\n{X}, {T}, Exile X cards from your graveyard: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nLook at the top seven cards of your library. Put two of them into your hand and the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', "Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nPut target nonland permanent on top of its owner's library.", 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nTarget creature gets +6/+6 until end of turn.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nTarget player sacrifices two creatures.', 'Delve (Each card you exile from your graveyard while casting this spell pays for {1}.)\\nTrample', 'Destroy all creatures and all permanents attached to creatures.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target attacking creature.', 'Destroy target blocking creature. Creatures that were blocked by that creature this combat gain trample until end of turn.', 'Destroy target creature with power 4 or greater.', 'Destroy target creature. If that creature had a +1/+1 counter on it, create a 1/1 green Snake creature token.', 'Dismal Backwater enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Dismal Backwater enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'Double strike\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Draw a card. Master the Way deals damage to any target equal to the number of cards in your hand.', 'Draw two cards.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0 and has "{2}{B}: Regenerate this creature."', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+4.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.', 'Enchant creature\\nWhen Singing Bell Strike enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn\'t untap during its controller\'s untap step.\\nEnchanted creature has "{6}: Untap this creature."', "Equipped creature gets +2/+2.\\nEquip {3}\\nGhostfire Blade's equip ability costs {2} less to activate if it targets a colorless creature.", 'Equipped creature has defender and "{2}, {T}: Other creatures you control gain trample and get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is this creature\'s power."\\nEquip {3}', 'Exile target enchantment.', 'Exile target nonland permanent.', 'Face-down creatures you control get +0/+1.\\nWhenever a permanent you control is turned face up, draw a card.', 'Ferocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, you may cast Dragon Grip as though it had flash. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nEnchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+0 and has first strike.', 'First strike, hexproof\\nWhenever Narset, Enlightened Master attacks, exile the top four cards of your library. Until end of turn, you may cast noncreature spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.', 'First strike\\nMorph {4}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'First strike\\nWhen Efreet Weaponmaster enters the battlefield or is turned face up, another target creature you control gets +3/+0 until end of turn.\\nMorph {2}{U}{R}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Flash\\nThis spell can't be countered.\\nCreature spells you control can't be countered.\\nOther creatures you control have trample.", "Flash\\nThis spell can't be countered.\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nReturn three lands you control to their owner's hand: Return Pearl Lake Ancient to its owner's hand.", 'Flying', 'Flying, first strike, haste', 'Flying, trample', 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying, vigilance, haste', 'Flying\\nHigh Sentinels of Arashin gets +1/+1 for each other creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.\\n{3}{W}: Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', "Flying\\nMorph {1}{G}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Icefeather Aven is turned face up, you may return another target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nMorph {2}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Mistfire Weaver is turned face up, target creature you control gains hexproof until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nMorph {3}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Flying\\nMorph {5}{U}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Thousand Winds is turned face up, return all other tapped creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Flying\\nMorph—Reveal a white card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Watcher of the Roost is turned face up, you gain 2 life.', 'Flying\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Flying\\nRaid — When Wingmate Roc enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, create a 3/4 white Bird creature token with flying.\\nWhenever Wingmate Roc attacks, you gain 1 life for each attacking creature.', 'Flying\\nSacrifice another creature: Butcher of the Horde gains your choice of vigilance, lifelink, or haste until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nSwarm of Bloodflies enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhenever another creature dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Swarm of Bloodflies.', 'Flying\\nWhen Ashcloud Phoenix dies, return it to the battlefield face down under your control.\\nMorph {4}{R}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Ashcloud Phoenix is turned face up, it deals 2 damage to each player.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Abomination of Gudul deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.\\nMorph {2}{B}{G}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Flying\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.', 'Flying\\n{2}{R}, Sacrifice Scaldkin: It deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Frontier Bivouac enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}, {U}, or {R}.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'Haste\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Haste\\nValley Dasher attacks each combat if able.', 'Haste\\nWhenever Ankle Shanker attacks, creatures you control gain first strike and deathtouch until end of turn.', "Haste\\nZurgo Helmsmasher attacks each combat if able.\\nZurgo Helmsmasher has indestructible as long as it's your turn.\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Zurgo Helmsmasher this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Zurgo Helmsmasher.", "Hexproof (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control.)\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)", 'Hooded Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nWhen Hooded Hydra dies, create a 1/1 green Snake creature token for each +1/+1 counter on it.\\nMorph {3}{G}{G}\\nAs Hooded Hydra is turned face up, put five +1/+1 counters on it.', "If a player would begin an extra turn, that player skips that turn instead.\\nIf Ugin's Nexus would be put into a graveyard from the battlefield, instead exile it and take an extra turn after this one.", 'If one or more +1/+1 counters would be put on a creature you control, that many plus one +1/+1 counters are put on it instead.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)\\nWhenever Meandering Towershell attacks, exile it. Return it to the battlefield under your control tapped and attacking at the beginning of the declare attackers step on your next turn.", 'Jungle Hollow enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Jungle Hollow enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nMorph {1}{B} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nMorph {2}{W}{B}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Look at the top four cards of your library. Put two of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard. You lose 2 life.', 'Mardu Skullhunter enters the battlefield tapped.\\nRaid — When Mardu Skullhunter enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, target opponent discards a card.', "Morph {2}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Jeering Instigator is turned face up, if it's your turn, gain control of another target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.", 'Morph {3}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {3}{W}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Master of Pearls is turned face up, creatures you control get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Morph {4}{B} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {4}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhenever Pine Walker or another creature you control is turned face up, untap that creature.', 'Morph {4}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Morph {4}{U}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Kheru Spellsnatcher is turned face up, counter target spell. If that spell is countered this way, exile it instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost for as long as it remains exiled.", 'Morph {4}{W} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {5} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {5}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Morph {B} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhenever another nontoken creature you control dies, draw a card.', "Morph—Reveal a blue card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Dragon's Eye Savants is turned face up, look at target opponent's hand.", 'Morph—Reveal a green card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Temur Charger is turned face up, target creature gains trample until end of turn.', 'Mystic Monastery enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {U}, {R}, or {W}.', "Mystic of the Hidden Way can't be blocked.\\nMorph {2}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)", 'Nomad Outpost enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {R}, {W}, or {B}.', 'Opulent Palace enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {B}, {G}, or {U}.', 'Other Warrior creatures you control get +0/+1.', 'Other Warrior creatures you control get +1/+0.', 'Outlast {1}{B} ({1}{B}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)', 'Outlast {1}{G} ({1}{G}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has reach. (A creature with reach can block creatures with flying.)', 'Outlast {1}{W} ({1}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)', 'Outlast {1}{W} ({1}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has first strike.', "Outlast {2}{W} ({2}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nWhenever you activate Herald of Anafenza's outlast ability, create a 1/1 white Warrior creature token.", 'Outlast {B} ({B}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has deathtouch.', 'Outlast {G} ({G}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has trample.', 'Outlast {W} ({W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has flying.', 'Outlast {W} ({W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has lifelink.', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever Jeskai Elder deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, Seeker of the Way gains lifelink until end of turn.', "Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. It gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn. (It can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, enchanted, or equipped by anything of that color.)", 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature, two +1/+1 counters on another target creature, and three +1/+1 counters on a third target creature.', 'Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature and untap it.', "Raid — War-Name Aspirant enters the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it if you attacked this turn.\\nWar-Name Aspirant can't be blocked by creatures with power 1 or less.", 'Raid — When Bellowing Saddlebrute enters the battlefield, you lose 4 life unless you attacked this turn.', 'Raid — When Mardu Heart-Piercer enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, Mardu Heart-Piercer deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Raid — When Mardu Hordechief enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, create a 1/1 white Warrior creature token.', 'Raid — When Mardu Warshrieker enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, add {R}{W}{B}.', 'Raid — When Timely Hordemate enters the battlefield, if you attacked this turn, return target creature card with mana value 2 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nMorph {4}{G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\nFerocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.", 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return up to two target creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Reveal the top eight cards of your library. You may put a creature card from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest into your graveyard.\\nFerocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, you may put two creature cards onto the battlefield instead of one.', 'Reveal the top five cards of your library. You may put a creature or land card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', 'Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rugged Highlands enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Sandsteppe Citadel enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}, {B}, or {G}.', 'Scoured Barrens enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Scoured Barrens enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Search your library for up to three basic land cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Surveil 5. (Look at the top five cards of your library, then put any number of them into your graveyard and the rest on top of your library in any order.)', 'Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Swiftwater Cliffs enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', "Tap X target creatures.\\nFerocious — If you control a creature with power 4 or greater, those creatures don't untap during their controllers' next untap steps.", "Tap target creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\nDraw a card.", 'Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains trample until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.', "Target creature you control fights target creature you don't control.\\nFerocious — The creature you control gets +2/+2 until end of turn before it fights if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.", "Target creature you control gets +1/+0 until end of turn. It fights target creature you don't control.", 'Target opponent discards two cards. Mill two cards.', 'Target opponent exiles the top X cards of their library. You may cast any number of spells with mana value X or less from among them without paying their mana costs.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a creature or planeswalker card from it. That player discards that card.', "The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. If damage is prevented this way, Deflecting Palm deals that much damage to that source's controller.", 'Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Thornwood Falls enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Trample, hexproof\\nMorph {3}{G}{U} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Trample\\nMorph {2}{G}{U}{R} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'Trample\\nWhen Siege Rhino enters the battlefield, each opponent loses 3 life and you gain 3 life.', 'Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Tranquil Cove enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Untap all creatures you control. They gain flying and double strike until end of turn.', "Untap each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it during each other player's untap step.", 'When Abzan Ascendancy enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.\\nWhenever a nontoken creature you control dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'When Armament Corps enters the battlefield, distribute two +1/+1 counters among one or two target creatures you control.', "When Bear's Companion enters the battlefield, create a 4/4 green Bear creature token.", 'When Highland Game dies, you gain 2 life.', 'When Mardu Blazebringer attacks or blocks, sacrifice it at end of combat.', 'When Ponyback Brigade enters the battlefield or is turned face up, create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.\\nMorph {2}{R}{W}{B} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', 'When Sultai Soothsayer enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the rest into your graveyard.', "When Suspension Field enters the battlefield, you may exile target creature with toughness 3 or greater until Suspension Field leaves the battlefield. (That creature returns under its owner's control.)", 'When Warden of the Eye enters the battlefield, return target noncreature, nonland card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nRaid — If you attacked this turn, when you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell an additional time. You may choose new targets for the copy.', "Whenever Anafenza, the Foremost attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on another target tapped creature you control.\\nIf a nontoken creature an opponent owns would die or a creature card not on the battlefield would be put into an opponent's graveyard, exile that card instead.", 'Whenever Avalanche Tusker attacks, target creature defending player controls blocks it this combat if able.', "Whenever Horde Ambusher blocks, it deals 1 damage to you.\\nMorph—Reveal a red card in your hand. (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Horde Ambusher is turned face up, target creature can't block this turn.", "Whenever Mardu Roughrider attacks, target creature can't block this turn.", 'Whenever Sidisi, Brood Tyrant enters the battlefield or attacks, mill three cards.\\nWhenever one or more creature cards are put into your graveyard from your library, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', 'Whenever a creature you control with toughness 4 or greater dies, each opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.\\n{2}{B}, Sacrifice another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Kheru Bloodsucker.', 'Whenever a creature you control with toughness 4 or greater dies, you gain 4 life.', "Whenever a face-down creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.\\nWhenever a permanent you control is turned face up, if it's a creature, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", "Whenever a nontoken creature you control attacks, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token that's tapped and attacking.\\nSacrifice Mardu Ascendancy: Creatures you control get +0/+3 until end of turn.", 'Whenever another permanent enters the battlefield under your control, each opponent mills a card.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, Heart-Piercer Bow deals 1 damage to target creature defending player controls.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever one or more cards are put into exile from your graveyard, put that many +1/+1 counters on Rakshasa Vizier.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn. Untap those creatures.\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token with haste.', "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, you may pay {1}. If you do, tap target creature an opponent controls and it doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Wind-Scarred Crag enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'Windstorm deals X damage to each creature with flying.', 'You gain 5 life.\\nFerocious — You gain 10 life instead if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', 'You may have Clever Impersonator enter the battlefield as a copy of any nonland permanent on the battlefield.', "You may look at the top card of your library and at face-down creatures you don't control any time.", '[+1]: Until end of turn, Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker becomes a legendary 4/4 red Dragon creature with flying, indestructible, and haste. (He doesn\'t lose loyalty while he\'s not a planeswalker.)\\n[−3]: Sarkhan, the Dragonspeaker deals 4 damage to target creature.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of your draw step, draw two additional cards" and "At the beginning of your end step, discard your hand."', '[+1]: Until your next turn, creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain lifelink.\\n[−2]: Create a 2/2 black Vampire creature token with flying.\\n[−6]: You get an emblem with "At the beginning of each opponent\'s upkeep, that player sacrifices a creature."', '{1}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Embodiment of Spring: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{1}{U}: Look at target face-down creature.', '{1}{W}: Unyielding Krumar gains first strike until end of turn.', '{2}, Exile Cranial Archive: Target player shuffles their graveyard into their library. Draw a card.', '{2}: Regenerate Kin-Tree Warden.\\nMorph {G} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)', "{2}{G}: Savage Knuckleblade gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.\\n{2}{U}: Return Savage Knuckleblade to its owner's hand.\\n{R}: Savage Knuckleblade gains haste until end of turn.", '{2}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{2}{W}: Leaping Master gains flying until end of turn.', '{3}{R}: Firehoof Cavalry gets +2/+0 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{B}, Remove X +1/+1 counters from among creatures you control: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn.', '{B}: Mardu Hateblade gains deathtouch until end of turn. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', '{B}{G}: Rakshasa Deathdealer gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\n{B}{G}: Regenerate Rakshasa Deathdealer.', '{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice Bloodstained Mire: Search your library for a Swamp or Mountain card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice Flooded Strand: Search your library for a Plains or Island card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice Polluted Delta: Search your library for an Island or Swamp card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice Windswept Heath: Search your library for a Forest or Plains card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}, Pay 1 life, Sacrifice Wooded Foothills: Search your library for a Mountain or Forest card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {B}, {G}, or {U}.\\n{B}{G}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Sultai Banner: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: You gain 1 life for each colorless creature you control.', '{T}: Add {G}, {U}, or {R}.\\nMorph {2} (You may cast this card face down as a 2/2 creature for {3}. Turn it face up any time for its morph cost.)\\nWhen Rattleclaw Mystic is turned face up, add {G}{U}{R}.', '{T}: Add {G}, {U}, or {R}.\\n{G}{U}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Temur Banner: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {R}, {W}, or {B}.\\n{R}{W}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Mardu Banner: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {U}, {R}, or {W}.\\n{U}{R}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Jeskai Banner: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {W}, {B}, or {G}.\\n{W}{B}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Abzan Banner: Draw a card.', '{U}: Scion of Glaciers gets +1/-1 until end of turn.']
flavor: ['"Anything a falcon can do, a bat can do in pitch darkness."\\n—Urdnan the Wanderer', '"Be as water: untamed and unheld, yet inexorably flowing toward a greater goal."\\n—Shensu, Riverwheel mystic', '"Bring down a stag and fix its horns upon her head. This one hears the whispers."\\n—Chianul, at the weaving of Arel', '"Death fills me and makes me strong. You, it will reduce to nothing."', '"Death is merely another foe the Mardu will overcome."', '"Do not think the sand or the sun will hold back the breath of winter."', '"Do you hear that, Sarkhan? The glory of the horde! I made a legend from what you abandoned."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Do you hunt the yetis of the high peaks, stripling? They are as fierce as the bear that fears no foe and as sly as the mink that creeps unseen. You will be as much prey as they."\\n—Nitula, the Hunt Caller', '"Even the greatest inferno begins as a spark. And anyone can snuff out a spark."\\n—Chanyi, mistfire sage', '"From your death, new life. From your loss, our profit."\\n—Kirada, Qarsi overseer', '"Have you spent a winter high in the mountains, where the ice walks and speaks to the wind? It is not a place for those who have not learned respect."\\n—Ulnok, Temur shaman', '"Here you lie then, Ugin. The corpses of worlds will join you in the tomb."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"Hold the high ground, then bring it to your enemy."\\n—Surrak, khan of the Temur', '"Hold the line, for family and the fallen!"', '"I am in my element: the element of surprise."\\n—Mogai, Sultai scout', '"I came seeking a challenge. All I found was you."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"I don\'t know where my destiny lies, but I know it isn\'t here."', '"I will wash you from my hooves!"\\n—Mardu taunt', '"If weakness does not exist within the Temur then we shall force it upon them."\\n—Sidisi, khan of the Sultai', '"Leave no scraps, lest you attract pests."\\n—Mardu threat', '"Let the world behold what becomes of those who defy us."\\n—Taigam, Sidisi\'s Hand', '"Make sure he\'s pointed in the right direction before you light him. And don\'t let the goblins anywhere near the torch."\\n—Kerai Suddenblade, Mardu hordechief', '"Many scales make the skin of a dragon."\\n—Abzan wisdom', '"Meat sustains the body. The spirit requires different sustenance."\\n—Arel the Whisperer', '"Naga shed their scales. We wear ours with pride."\\n—Golran, dragonscale captain', '"No body can contain so much fury. It reminds me of another battle, long past."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"No one petal claims beauty for the lotus."', '"Only the weak imprison themselves behind walls. We live free under the wind, and our freedom makes us strong."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Our own selves are the greatest obstacles to enlightenment."\\n—Narset, khan of the Jeskai', '"People are often humbled by the elements. But the elements, too, can be humbled."\\n—Surrak, khan of the Temur', '"See your enemies from a thousand sides. Then you will find a thousand ways to kill them."', '"Soldiers win battles, but supplies win wars."\\n—Kadri, Abzan caravan master', '"Stand where the whole battle can see you. Strike so they\'ll never forget."\\n—Anafenza, khan of the Abzan', '"Strength batters down barriers. Discipline ignores them."', '"Strike," the fumes hiss. "Raise an empire with your ambition."', '"The Abzan replaced my savagery with a noble heritage. I would give my life for my House."', '"The Houses always hope for peace, but we always pack for war."\\n—Gvar Barzeel, krumar commander', '"The Jeskai would have me bow in restraint. So I have found a people unafraid of true power."', '"The Sultai came hunting for a bear hide. Now I have a belt of naga skin, and my friend has a full belly."', '"The Sultai take our dead, so we shall take their living!"\\n—Taklai, Mardu ragesinger', '"The Way has no beginning and no end. It is simply the path."\\n—Narset, khan of the Jeskai', '"The amber of the tree and the blood of my veins are the same."', '"The arrow strikes one bird down, but the flock remains."\\n—Jeskai teaching', '"The best servants are made from those who died without a scratch."\\n—Sidisi, khan of the Sultai', '"The dragons thought they were too strong to be tamed, too large to fall. And where are they now?"\\n—Khibat the Revered', '"The man whom I call father killed the orc who sired me, offering his world and his blade in return."', '"The most powerful dreams visit those who shelter in a dragon\'s skull."\\n—Chianul, Who Whispers Twice', '"The mountains scream with the dragons\' throats."\\n—Chianul, Who Whispers Twice', '"The past and the unwritten are frozen. To understand their meaning requires heat."\\n—Arel the Whisperer', '"The stronger our enemies seem, the more vulnerable they are."\\n—Sultai secret', '"The voice calls me here, yet I see only bones. Is this more dragon trickery?"\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"There are no obstacles, only different paths."', '"There is nothing so free as the spring river born of winter\'s ice."\\n—Nitula, the Hunt Caller', '"There may be little honor in my tactics, but there is no honor in losing."', '"These roads are desolate and changeable. Follow me, or die in the wastes."', '"They thought their fortress impregnable . . . until we marched up with ours, and blocked out the sun."\\n—Golran, dragonscale captain', '"Those who have never ridden before the wind do not know the true joy of war."', '"To conquer is to eat."\\n—Edicts of Ilagra', '"Truth is hard enough to see, let alone understand. We must remove all distractions to find clarity."\\n—Zogye, wandering sage', '"Unwelcome thoughts crowd my mind. Are they my own madness, or the whispers of another?"\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Water shifts and confuses, but as ice it holds the stillness of truth."\\n—Arel the Whisperer', '"We all want to know what\'s going on in someone else\'s head. I simply open it up and look."', '"We are the flicker of the flame and its heat, the two sides of a single blade."', '"We are the shield unbroken. If we fall today, we will die well, and our trees will bear our names in honor."', '"We are the swift, the strong, the blade\'s sharp shriek! Fear nothing, and strike!"', '"We have a word for enemies too mutilated for military service: furniture."\\n—Taigam, Sidisi\'s Hand', '"What warrior worth the name fears to leave a trail? If my enemies seek me, let them follow the ashes in my wake."', '"When the last dragon fell, its spirit escaped as a roar into the wind."\\n—Temur tale', '"When we were lost and weary, the ainok showed us how to survive. They have earned the right to call themselves Abzan, and to wear the Scale."\\n—Anafenza, khan of the Abzan', '"Wherever I walk, the ancestors walk too."', '"You are beneath contempt. Your lineage will be forgotten."', '"You can have the body, necromancer. I just want the skin."', '"You have returned from fire, traitor. This time I will see you leave as ashes."\\n—Zurgo, to Sarkhan Vol', '"Your corruption will burn, serpent, until there is nothing left to defile."\\n—Asmala, bloodfire mystic', 'A band of Temur hunters, fleeing the Mardu, dug a hideout beneath such a creature as it slept. The horde found them and attacked. For three days the Temur held them at bay, and all the while the great beast slumbered.', 'Abzan ancestors died to protect their Houses, and they protect them still.', 'Abzan soldiers march to war confident that their Houses march with them.', 'Adepts of the Riverwheel Stronghold can run through rain and never get wet; masters use the raindrops as stepping stones.', "All at once Sarkhan's mind fell silent.", "Arel dreamed of winter's end. The next morning she followed a strange trail and found a seedling in the snow.", 'As a test of calm and compassion, a Jeskai monk softly approaches a grazing sambar and offers it a lotus from his or her hand. If the creature eats, the student ascends to the next level of training.', 'Both his rank and his scars were earned in single combat against a cave bear.', 'Countless delights drift on the surface while dark schemes run below.', 'Crude tactics can be effective nonetheless.', 'Designed by an ancient artificer, the finest Mardu bows are carved from dragon bone and strung with the wind itself.', 'Discipline is the first pillar of the Jeskai Way. Each member of the clan trains in a weapon, perfecting its use over a lifetime.', 'Discipline to persevere, insight to discover.', 'Do not fear the lightning. Fear the one it obeys.', 'Dragons are extinct on Tarkir, but Abzan magic still emulates their endurance.', 'Enduring the most desolate and dangerous conditions, Abzan sentries unfailingly guard the stronghold gates.', 'Even among the hardiest warriors of the Temur, loxodons are respected for their adaptation to the mountain snows.', 'Every shaft is graven with a name from a kin tree, calling upon the spirits of the ancestors to make it fly true.', 'First the thunder, then the rain.', 'Flesh wounds are meaningless to those who discard their flesh so readily.', 'Goblins, like snowflakes, are only dangerous in numbers.', 'Gold buys death. Death earns gold.', 'Got a diving lesson\\n—Sultai expression meaning "was fed to the crocodiles"', 'Her palm flared like the eye of a waking dragon. Then all was calm.', "His arrows whistle like a serpent's hiss.", "If you fear the dragon's fire, you are unworthy to wield it.", 'In the Gudul delta, bloodfly bites are indistinguishable from spear wounds.', 'In the high caves of the Qal Sisma mountains, young hunters quest to hear the echoes of their fierce ancestors.', 'In the silence of the ice, even dreams become still.', 'Interlopers in Sultai territory usually end up as crocodile chow or baboon bait.', 'It stares through the empty, pain-twisted faces of those it has drained.', 'It strode through the clash of dragons, the fall of Ugin, and the rise of the khans.', 'Its hunting instincts have long since rotted away. Its hunger, however, remains.', 'Its wings produce a high-pitched, barely audible whirring sound in flight. Only Jeskai masters are quiet enough to hear one coming.', 'Lammasu are the enigmatic travelers of Tarkir, soaring high above all lands in all seasons. None know their true purpose, but they often arrive on the eve of great conflicts or turning points in history.', 'Lightning burns its own path.', 'Long after death, the spirits of the Disowned continue to seek redemption among their Abzan kin.', 'Mantis riders know their mounts owe them no allegiance. Even a mantis ridden for years would consume a rider who loses focus for only a moment.', 'Mardu archers are trained in Dakla, the way of the bow. They never miss their target, no matter how small, how fast, or how far away.', "Mardu riders' greatest fear is that a battle might end before their weapons draw blood.", 'Mastodons became extinct long ago, but foul forces of the Gurmag Swamp sometimes animate their decaying remains. The Sultai happily exploit such creatures but consider them inferior to their own necromantic creations.', 'No battle means more to a Mardu warrior than the one that earns her war name.', 'One quiet word sets off the stampede.', 'Power to dominate, cruelty to rule.', 'Rakshasa offer deals that sound advantageous to those who forget who they are dealing with.', 'Rakshasa trade in secrets, amassing wealth from their careful revelation.', 'Rarely at rest on the Amber Throne, Anafenza always leads the Abzan Houses to battle.', 'Savagery to survive, courage to triumph.', "Shintan sensed the malice in his opponent, but he did not strike until the orc's muscles tensed in preparation to throw the first punch.", 'Since they guard armies of walking carrion, Sultai aven are never far from a meal.', 'Some ainok of the mountains are accepted among the Temur as trusted hunt-mates.', 'Some efreet abandon their homes in the volcanic Fire Rim to embrace the Jeskai Way and discipline their innate flames.', 'Speed to strike, fury to smash.', 'Stone to endure, roots to remember.', 'Supplicants offer flesh and silver, flowers and blood. The altar takes what it will, eyes gleaming with unspoken promises.', 'Sure-footed, strong-willed, and ill-tempered—and so is the ram.', 'Temur shamans speak of three destinies: the now, the echo of the past, and the unwritten. They find flickering paths among tangled possibilities.', 'That which endures, survives.', 'The Abzan avoid extended supply lines by incorporating weapons stores into their battle formations.', 'The Abzan turn to this spell only as a last resort, for its inevitable result is what they most dread: to be alone.', "The Mardu charge reflects the dragon's speed—and its hunger.", "The Sagu Jungle's thick undergrowth conceals even the largest predators—if they wish to remain hidden.", 'The Sultai distinguish between pet and slave by the material of the chain.', 'The Sultai would rebuild the empire on the backs of the dead.', 'The Temur believe that scaldkin are born when eruptions melt the frozen whispers of sleeping ancestors.', 'The Temur believe three things only are needed in life: a hot fire, a full belly, and a strong companion.', 'The Temur call the flickering lights the Path of Whispers, believing that they lead the way to ancestral knowledge.', 'The Temur have no patience for subtlety.', 'The Temur welcome bears into the clan, fighting alongside them in battle. The relationship dates back to when they labored side by side under Sultai rule.', "The adept underwent months of preparation to withstand pain, until he was finally ready to receive the efreet master's teachings.", 'The appearance of a kirin signifies the passing or arrival of an important figure. As word of sightings spread, all the khans took it to mean themselves. Only the shaman Chianul thought of Sarkhan Vol.', 'The blades of a Sultai assassin stab like the fangs of a dragon.', 'The bonds of family cross the boundaries of race.', 'The broken Qal Sisma foothills make poor terrain for cavalry, but a perfect setting for ambushes.', 'The calligraphy of combat is written with strokes of sudden blood.', "The crocodiles' putrid jaws swallow everything but the screams.", 'The dense jungle surrenders to a lush and lavish expanse. At its center uncoil the spires of Qarsi Palace.', 'The envoy spoke, and Sidisi replied.', 'The fastest way across the dunes is above.', "The greatest idea the zombie ever had in its head wasn't even its own.", 'The horde grows with each assault.', 'The mere approach of an Abzan war beast is enough to send enemies fleeing in panic.', 'The most ferocious saddlebrutes lead the assault, ramming through massed pikes and stout barricades as if they were paper and silk.', 'The naga of the Sultai Brood made deals with dark forces to keep their power.', "The ogre's mind snapped. The bow was next. The archer followed quickly after.", "The passing years add new rings to the tree's trunk, bolstering the spirits that dwell within.", 'The remains of ancient sky tyrants now feed the war-torn land.', 'The stature of the fighter matters less than the depth of the cut.', 'The voice of a rakshasa is soft, its breath sweet. But every word is the murmur of madness.', "The wardens guard the sacred documents of Tarkir's history, though they are forbidden to read the words.", 'There are many Jeskai styles: Riverwalk imitates flowing water, Dragonfist the ancient hellkites, and Flying Crane the wild aven of the high peaks.', 'These winged warriors meditate in flight, tracing mandalas in the clouds.', 'They range from Sage-Eye Stronghold to the farthest reaches of Tarkir.', 'Victory is certain. The price, negotiable.', 'What once soared high above Tarkir is now reduced to a seat.', 'When Anafenza holds court under the First Tree, the gates of Mer-Ek are sealed. No safer place exists in all of Tarkir.', 'When Temur warriors enter the battle trance known as "awakening the bear," they lose all sense of enemy or friend, seeing only threats to the wilderness.', 'When asked how many paths reach enlightenment, the monk kicked a heap of sand. "Count," he smiled, "and then find more grains."', 'Where an enemy once rode, not even a whisper remains.', 'Where dragons once prevailed, their bones now sink.', 'Where dragons once roared, their bones now keen.', 'Where dragons once slept, their bones now rest.', 'Where dragons once triumphed, their bones now molder.', "Where dragons' breath once burned, their bones now freeze."]
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Gaillet', 'David Palumbo', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Evan Shipard', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'James Zapata', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jasper Sandner', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Winters', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Stewart', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Mike Bierek', 'Min Yum', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Richard Wright', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Torstein Nordstrand', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'YW Tang', 'Yefim Kligerman', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zack Stella', 'Zoltan Boros']
